course: dictionary
lesson: 4633
title: Hind: back legs or a deer?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hind is a word with two jobs. Most of the time it is an adjective, which describes something, and it means at the back. You will mostly see it in the phrase hind legs. «The Kangaroo stands up on his back legs and hops, and his hind legs grow longer and stronger with every bound.» Here the back legs and the hind legs are the same legs.
explain: Context gives you the clue. «She grabs him by a fore-leg and a hind-leg» tells you that a fore-leg is at the front and a hind-leg is at the back. Fore means front and hind means back, so the two words are opposites. Try the swap test: put back in place of hind and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Hind can also be a noun, which names a thing. A hind is a female red deer, and its plural is hinds. Look at the words around it: if it is a noun, it will be a thing or an animal, not a description of one. Hind legs has hind before a noun, so it is an adjective there.
fact: Hind is an adjective, and it means at the back.
fact: Hind legs are the back legs of an animal, like the back legs of a dog.
fact: Kangaroos and frogs jump with strong hind legs.
fact: A hind is a noun that means a female red deer.
fact: In the phrase «talk the hind legs off a donkey», hind legs is part of an idiom. In the UK it means talk too much.
exercise: What does hind mean in «his hind legs grow longer and stronger»? | Hidden | Front | Very tired | *At the back
exercise: «She grabs him by a fore-leg and a hind-leg.» Which leg is at the front? | *Fore-leg | Both legs | Hind-leg | Neither leg
exercise: Ben says his gran can talk the hind legs off a donkey. What does this mean? | *She talks too much | She has lost her donkey | She rides donkeys | She is very strong
test: In science, the dog's hind legs are the ones that... | Are made of wood | *Are at the back of its body | Are at the front of its body | Hold the ball
test: Which animals jump with strong hind legs? | Snails | *Kangaroos and frogs | Fish | Owls
exam: Hind is an adjective meaning at the back, but it is also a noun. What is a hind? | A front leg | *A female red deer | A kind of bird | Another name for a donkey
